## Criticisms (criticisms)
[024336743e984913] (mini.criticism.v1)
The single expectation in this cycle failed. The proposal predicted that adding 'I cannot' after a fenced JSON object would move response-verdict from JSON_OBJECT to refusal, because it read H36 as making a refusal phrase override a recovered object. The execution shows the check returned JSON_OBJECT both before and after the edit: response-verdict unchanged, expected moves. No inputs were thrown away; the pair was validated against its cell and executed. The check's behavior is consistent with the rule's first clause, 'The refusal heuristic decides the verdict only when no object can be recovered.' H36 only says the refusal phrase is recorded beside a recovered object, not that it changes the verdict. So this pair does not demonstrate a defect. A proposer should next target the no-object branch: make one text contain no recoverable JSON object and no refusal phrase, and the edited text add a refusal phrase, expecting the verdict to move to refusal; or test recovery precedence where a final unparseable object is passed over and an earlier draft parses, since the rule says the last object is scored but also says unparseable candidates are passed over.

